	quest.691ED51F3749B8C1.quest_subtitle: "Craft Crook"
	quest.695D12876E96C195.quest_desc: [
		"In a vast world of blocks suspended in mid-air, known as Lidotech, the floating islands weren't filled with wild forests, but with machines, pipes, and automated systems. Trees had been replaced by generators, and rivers by networks of industrial power and fluids."
		""
		"At the center of this world lived a small, pixelated explorer named you. You were one of the few survivors capable of understanding the ancient technologies left behind by industrial civilizations and getting them working again."
		""
		"In Lidotech, players had to rebuild the world piece by piece, using mods like Create and Thermal Expansion, to transform empty islands into veritable flying factories."
		""
		"One day, a vital production chain began to grind to a halt. The machines weren't receiving enough power, the resource transport systems were jammed, and the industrial sky islands were losing their balance."
		""
		"You were sent to explore the heights and find the cause of the problem."
		""
		"He traversed floating platforms connected by mechanical bridges, where giant gears spun slowly in mid-air. The further he ventured, the more complex installations he discovered, using abandoned conveyors, engines, and automated systems."
		""
		"At the summit of a forgotten island, he found the heart of the industrial network: an ancient control structure still using Create and Industrial Mods systems, but poorly powered and partially deactivated."
		""
		"Rather than rebuild everything, he reconnected the power lines, rebalanced the resource flows, and restarted the machines one by one."
		""
		"Gradually, the islands came back to life. The conveyors began turning again, the factories started producing once more, and the sky systems regained their stability."
		""
		"But he knew that Lidotech was vast, and that many islands remained to be explored, filled with forgotten machines and industrial secrets waiting to be uncovered."
		""
		"And so, he set off again into the sky, towards new floating factories still silent, ready to rebuild the world, block by block."
	]
